    "time_horizon": "long-term",
    "confidence": "moderate",
    "plain": "Banning fracking and new coal mines removes two sources of greenhouse gas emissions, pollution, and seismic risk, helping protect the climate and environment over the long term. The near-term environmental gain is modest since the fracking ban was already in place and coal power has ended, but the long-term signal is clearly positive.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the ban on coking coal genuinely reduces global emissions or merely shifts production and imports from elsewhere, leaving net CO2 unchanged.",
