        "quote": "The Royal College of Physicians welcomed the ban as a \"crucial step forward in protecting the health and well-being of current and future generations,\" citing coal combustion's link to cardiovascular and respiratory diseases."
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "Expert consensus holds that fracking would not significantly reduce UK energy bills or enhance energy security in the short to medium term.",
        "evidence_id": "E3",
        "quote": "A strong consensus among scientists and economists, including the Grantham Institute, Imperial College London, Newcastle University, and Durham University, indicates that fracking would not significantly reduce UK energy bills or enhance energy security in the short to medium term."
      }
